                        {# The teacher's tool menu (handoff design_handoff_menu_outils): ONE flat panel,
                           no submenu, split into three named groups - what one runs live in class,
                           what one prepares beforehand, what one follows up afterwards. Text labels
                           only, no icons, per the main-menu rule.

                           Some of these tools are multi-class by nature and open straight from here
                           (audio recordings, progression, the sequence and quiz libraries, the student
                           work list); the others only work on one class and go through
                           App\Controller\ToolsController's picker first, since the top bar does not
                           know which class is meant. Reached from a class's own submenu instead, they
                           get it from the URL and never pass through the picker.

                           Gated to teachers and staff, not merely "not a student": every entry here
                           is a teaching tool, and its own controller already refuses anyone else -
                           showing the menu to, say, a tutor only bought them a 403.

                           Namesake of the student "Outils" menu further down, which has nothing to do
                           with this one - the two never show for the same person. #}
                        {# Every group carries its own boolean, and the menu itself is the union of
                           the three: a header with nothing under it and a menu that opens on
                           nothing are the same defect, and both become reachable as soon as an
                           establishment switches a few of these off. #}
